add('''<h2 id="universe">A broader universe with visible boundaries</h2>
<p>The CDER compilation contains 1,387 original approvals in 1985–2025. Of 924 approvals in the 2000–2025 primary period, 380 have at least one original orphan-designated use. Partial orphan designation was retained. The live CBER roster contributes 55 products, screened separately; its relevant original dates were checked on product pages.</p>
<p>The resulting clinical shortlist contains <strong>27 first-approved-DMT candidates, 38 prior-care boundaries and 17 adjacent or DMT-uncertain therapies</strong> in the primary period. These are provisional clinical categories, not 82 confirmed eligible first DMTs. Thirteen pre-2000 precedents and four verified 2026 entrants are retained separately, making 99 extended candidate/control entries. The US orphan designation is used as an initial rarity proxy (normally fewer than 200,000 US patients, with a statutory cost-recovery exception); exception status and actual accessible population require separate adjudication.</p>''')
