add('''<div class="callout caution"><strong>This is not an exhaustive historical first-DMT census.</strong> The OOPD request returned a search form rather than a usable approval export. Original-NME data omit some repurposed drugs, first rare indications approved as supplements and non-NMEs. The current CBER list can omit historical withdrawals. The 544 non-orphan-designated original approvals were not all clinically adjudicated for rarity. These gaps prevent population-wide inference.</div>
<p>Representative omitted-route checks include Fintepla, Ravicti, Procysbi and Cystadrops. Most are likely symptomatic or followers, but that is not a justification for assuming every missing approval is ineligible. A full orphan export, non-NME/supplement reconciliation and historical biologics list are the right next route to complete the denominator.</p>
<p>The focus on chronic genetic/metabolic/CNS disease also excludes acute infections, supportive/diagnostic interventions and tumor settings. This goes beyond the original oncology exclusion and is disclosed as a scope narrowing. Withdrawn or disappointing products are not deleted for their outcomes: Oxbryta, Relyvrio and Adakveo remain visible as follower/control records.</p>''')
