add('''<p><strong>What the three 2004 observations establish:</strong> an identifiable sell-side analyst published specific preapproval annual expectations that were below later reported product sales. They improve on unsourced peak anecdotes. They do not establish how many other analysts agreed, whether the estimates were probability-weighted, or whether the expected territory/age mix matched actual sales.</p>
<p><strong>What the countercases establish:</strong> first-entry ERT status is compatible with an approximately realized expectation or a major shortfall. Vimizim's estimate was made much closer to approval than the 2004 cluster. Kanuma's number was attributed to Cortellis rather than a named sell-side analyst. Differences in vintage and source type are reasons to stratify, not reasons to discard unfavorable observations.</p>
<p>Kanuma's source called $603m a peak in a specified year, 2020. The comparison uses that stated target year; no annual curve was constructed. Vimizim's source said annual sales “by 2017,” treated here as a target-year quotation with that wording preserved. No later disease indication is needed to calculate these five checks, although expected age/phenotype and territory scope remain unresolved.</p>
<h3>Probability sensitivity without inventing probabilities</h3>
<div class="formula">If quoted F = p × conditional forecast, then conditional error = p × A/F − 1.<br>The break-even probability is p* = F/A.</div>''')
add(table(['2004 case','Break-even scalar PoS','Interpretation'],[[p['product'],f'{p["break_even_scalar_pos"]:.1%}','Raw beat remains a conditional beat only if the true multiplier exceeds this threshold.'] for p in e['new_target_year_comparisons'] if p['break_even_scalar_pos'] is not None]))
add('''<p>These thresholds are not estimates of the original models' PoS. For example, a hypothetical 30% multiplier would reverse the Naglazyme comparison despite its large raw beat. Conversely, if Kanuma's quoted estimate were risk-weighted by a scalar no greater than 100%, undoing that multiplier would make its conditional forecast larger and the shortfall more severe, assuming the other scope matches held.</p>
<p>Geography can also reverse the sign: Naglazyme's reported 2007 global revenue was $86.2m, but US revenue derives to $17.5m after subtracting $68.7m ex-US. That is why a worldwide actual cannot be casually matched to an unspecified forecast. The common 2004 publication also includes five already marketed products; all eight rows are retained in the extraction record rather than selecting only favorable preapproval outcomes.</p>
<h3>What can and cannot be aggregated</h3>
<p><strong>Five new raw comparisons; three from one analyst publication; zero strict 36-month curves; zero strict 60-month curves.</strong> No pooled beat rate, median “bias,” confidence interval or uplift is reported. The five cases mix earlier-stage and near-approval vintages and several source types. A simple fraction above forecast would answer a question about these accessible excerpts, not a representative first-DMT cohort.</p>''')
