add('''<h2 id="cmp">What this means for CMP-002</h2>
<p>CMP-002 is a repeat intrathecal ASO intended to raise SYNGAP1 expression through regulatory-RNA targeting. As of the November5 2026 company update, first patient dosing in ASCEND was planned for year-end; human clinical efficacy is not yet established. It should be called a <strong>potential first DMT</strong>, with first-at-launch status and disease-modifying benefit treated as hypotheses.</p>
<p>The September28 2026 trial design includes ages 2 to under18, specified truncating mutations in exons5–19, and substantial seizure-related entry criteria. Those are trial eligibility rules, not an approved future label or the whole disease prevalence. Missense/nontruncating variants, microdeletions and other excluded groups cannot be silently counted as proven commercial candidates. Conversely, the eventual label should not be assumed permanently identical to the first trial.</p>
<p>Current SYNGAP1 care includes antiseizure medicines, rescue treatment, selected dietary/device approaches and developmental support. Thus, first DMT would enter an existing clinical and caregiver ecosystem. Incremental value must be assessed across seizures and broader development/function rather than treating the population as wholly untreated.</p>''')
add('<p class="sources">'+link('camp_update','CAMP4 November5 2026 update')+' · '+link('camp_8k','September28 2026 SEC trial-design disclosure')+' · '+link('chop','CHOP SYNGAP1 care overview')+'.</p>')
add('''<p>The patient-organization publication reports a March31 2024 census of 1,400 known patients worldwide and discusses 401 counted in the US. These are dated ascertainment counts, not 2026 prevalence. It also describes a modeled de novo incidence of 6.107 per100,000 births, composed of 0.787 truncating and 5.320 missense variants. The mismatch between modeled variant incidence and the diagnosed cohort is unresolved. Total predicted incidence therefore cannot be multiplied by population and treated as the eligible market for a trial focused on specified truncating variants.</p>
<p>Stoke's August2026 update says lead optimization was underway for a SYNGAP1 clinical candidate. It is direct evidence that eventual first-mover status and competitive durability cannot be assumed. The current review is not an exhaustive competitor census. Likewise, the primary trial-design source used here is CAMP4's SEC disclosure; an official trial-registry record was not independently reconciled in this pass.</p>''')
add('<p class="sources">'+link('syngap_census','SYNGAP1 patient-organization census and incidence discussion')+' · '+link('stoke','Stoke August3 2026 pipeline update')+'.</p>')
add('''<h3>The commercial model should expose six separate mechanisms</h3>''')
add(table(['Model component','Upside hypothesis','Disconfirming observation / downside','Historical guide'],[
 ['Findable patient pool','Better genetic testing identifies previously unrecognized eligible patients.','Low diagnostic yield, inaccessible records, noneligible genotypes or few referrals despite testing.','Kanuma; Ztalmy; Mepsevii'],
 ['Clinical eligibility and benefit','Meaningful benefit extends across age/function groups.','Older or severe patients have little reversible benefit; evidence/label narrows scope.','Lenmeldy; Nulibry; Luxturna; Myozyme'],
 ['Initiation and capacity','Specialist networks convert identified patients efficiently.','Procedure slots, travel, sedation or caregiver burden delay starts.','Spinraza; Brineura; Kebilidi'],
 ['Exposure and continuation','Patients sustain meaningful benefit and continue treatment.','Interruptions, discontinuation, missed procedures or perceived limited benefit reduce paid exposure.','Daybue; Ztalmy; repeated CNS therapies'],
 ['Net economics and territories','Payer access and international rollout support value capture.','Rebates, free drug, lower country prices, rights structure or delayed reimbursement erode revenue.','Myalept; Naglazyme; Elaprase'],
 ['Competitive durability','First entrant remains preferred with a durable clinical advantage.','New routes/mechanisms shift starts or switch existing patients.','Spinraza; Arcalyst; NPC boundary cases']]))
add('''<div class="formula">Paid revenue in a period = Σ (treated patient-months × net revenue per treated month)<br>Patient starts are constrained by eligibility, referral, willingness, reimbursement and procedure capacity.<br>Continuing exposure follows cohort-specific discontinuation, interruptions and survival.</div>
<p>This avoids multiplying a single prevalence figure by several overlapping “penetration,” “adherence” and “persistence” discounts. Separate newly diagnosed patients from an existing backlog and incident births. Model each territory's launch/reimbursement date and economic rights. Do not transplant enzyme weight-based pricing into an ASO without a dosing rationale.</p>
<p>The supplied Needham model already assumes diagnosis rises from 15% to 50%, 50% penetration of diagnosed patients, 75% adherence/persistence and 15% GTN; its $2.106bn conditional peak has 25% PoS applied in valuation. Therefore, “analysts omit diagnosis expansion” is not an adequate critique of that model. The independent task is to test whether the timing, denominator, eligible fractions and continuation assumptions are right. These Street assumptions remain context, not inputs used to choose this historical cohort.</p>
<p>Historical evidence can enter the model now as structural constraints and named upside/downside scenarios. It does not yet justify an empirically calibrated penetration, GTN or persistence uplift. Preclinical functional rescue cannot fill that gap. The separate reverse-DCF project should compare the market-implied commercial curve with a separately built epidemiology model, while allowing financing, development costs, dilution, timing and other pipeline value to explain a gap. A sales gap alone is not proof of undervaluation.</p>''')
add('<p class="sources">Street assumptions are documented in '+filelink('data/research_evidence.json','the prior source-verified CAMP evidence package')+' and the preserved Needham report; no new valuation is calculated here.</p>')
add('''<h2 id="claims">Which investor claims are defensible?</h2>''')
add(table(['Claim','Assessment','Evidence needed to strengthen it'],[
 ['“Analysts systematically underforecast first rare-disease DMTs.”','Not established. The available comparisons are nonrepresentative and not risk/scope matched.','A reconciled universe and timestamped original annual curves with known conditionality.'],
 ['“Several early ERT sales forecasts were substantially below subsequently reported sales.”','Supported as a qualified raw historical observation from one original analyst publication.','Underlying model geography, PoS, price and patient assumptions; independent analysts for the same cases.'],
 ['“A first therapy automatically unlocks the undiagnosed population.”','Not supported; Kanuma is direct disconfirming operational evidence.','Longitudinal tests → diagnoses → eligible referrals → starts, with cost and time per conversion.'],
 ['“A diagnosed population can still expand commercially through territory/access changes.”','Plausible and supported as a mechanism; magnitude not isolated.','Country patient/exposure data and the original forecast rollout schedule.'],
 ['“First DMT and clinical benefit make later competitors unimportant.”','Not supported. Product share and disease-market growth are different.','Competitor timing, relative benefit, switching and administration preferences.'],
 ['“CMP-002 has underappreciated upside if diagnosis, eligibility or durable benefit exceeds current assumptions.”','A valid conditional hypothesis, not a demonstrated valuation conclusion.','Independent epidemiology, genotype/function segmentation, human evidence, access/capacity economics and market-implied curve.']]))
add('''<p>A defensible narrative would say: historical first rare-disease launches show that commercial outcomes depend on identifiable assumptions about the reachable population, treatment exposure and access. Some early replacement-therapy estimates were too low; other first therapies disappointed. CMP-002's potential upside should be demonstrated through those specific assumptions and supported by human evidence, rather than asserted from rarity or first-mover status.</p>
<h2 id="next">Highest-value missing data and stopping rule</h2>
<p>The bottleneck is original annual forecast models and matching fields, not another collection of peak-sales headlines. No outreach has been initiated. The following is a concrete acquisition specification for existing institutional access or later authorized collection.</p>''')
add(table(['Priority','Exact request','Why it has high information value'],[
 ['1 — resolve the new cluster','SG Cowen / Yaron Werber LSD models underlying Jan.2004 Table1; BioMarin/Naglazyme, Genzyme/Myozyme and TKT/I2S coverage. Retrieve annual revenue, territory, patient, price, launch and PoS equations.','Three authentic preapproval observations share a source; one set of original assumptions can resolve whether the strongest apparent beats survive normalization.'],
 ['2 — recover independent same-case forecasts','For Naglazyme (approval May31 2005), Myozyme (Apr28 2006) and Elaprase (Jul24 2006), obtain each bank’s nearest 9–15-month preapproval model, then latest preapproval model.','Separates one analyst/early-vintage cluster from a reproducible disease-level pattern. Do not select the lowest estimate.'],
 ['3 — balance with neutral/downside cases','Bloomberg constituent Vimizim models behind Nov21 2013 $416m/2017; Cortellis contributors and model behind May6 2015 Kanuma $603m/2020; also their primary-vintage snapshots.','Resolves source composition and geography with symmetric retrieval rather than searching only successful drugs.'],
 ['4 — match closest CNS analogues','Spinraza 2015–2016 and Brineura 2016–2017 full annual models; identify original forecasts before pivotal results separately.','Most relevant to repeated CNS treatment; obtain starts, loading/maintenance, eligible age and procedure assumptions.'],
 ['5 — identify clinic and net-price mechanisms','CDD-only Ztalmy 2021/early2022; Rett-only Daybue 2022/early2023; Myalept 2013–2014; Mepsevii 2016–2017.','Separate neurodevelopmental adoption, tolerability, tiny-population dynamics and GTN without requiring all to be strict DMTs.'],
 ['6 — complete the sampling denominator','Usable OOPD approved-drug export, non-NME/supplement reconciliation and historical CBER biologics/withdrawal records.','Needed before claiming a representative universe or estimating a population bias.'],
 ['7 — observable operational validation','Deidentified aggregate testing yield from genetic labs; registry enrollment and genotype/age counts; center procedure throughput; specialty-pharmacy paid exposure; payer mix and authorization delays.','These observers measure the actual conversion process. No patient-level data or outreach is assumed authorized.']]))
add('''<p>Required fields for each forecast: exact timestamp, analyst/bank, original model or page, drug and disease, geographic rights, nominal currency, annual net-sales curve, launch assumptions, population/price/exposure drivers, label/age/genotype scope and where PoS enters. Obtain corresponding monthly/quarterly actuals, country splits, free-drug treatment, licensing revenue and disclosure changes. Keep failed retrievals as missing observations.</p>
<p>After acquisition, predefine equal-weight drug-level aggregation and rerun first-status, vintage, geography, unchanged-label and leave-one-source-family-out sensitivities. If scope cannot be reconciled, retain the case as mechanism evidence. Do not fit a pooled regression to a handful of heterogeneous excerpts. The current public-source pass stops here because additional generic searching is unlikely to repair the missing model fields.</p>
<h2>Deliverables, checks and reproducibility</h2>
<p>Arithmetic was recomputed from stored numbers; frame counts and source references were reconciled; no unknown PoS was filled; every original 2004 table row was retained; and every new comparison remains excluded from the strict cumulative sample. These checks establish internal consistency, not independent validation of clinical similarity or causal attribution.</p>''')
add('<ul>'+''.join('<li>'+filelink(p,l)+'</li>' for p,l in [('data/independent/evidence.json','Structured case evidence, source registry and data dictionary'),('data/independent/forecast_actuals.csv','Forecast/actual comparison CSV'),('data/independent/analogue_matrix.csv','Analogue matrix CSV'),('data/independent/approval_screen.csv','Full approval-screen CSV'),('data/independent/approval_screen.json','1,442-row regulatory disposition ledger'),('data/independent/candidate_universe.json','99-entry extended candidate universe'),('data/independent/validation.json','Recomputed counts, arithmetic and matching checks'),('protocol/independent_deviations_and_coverage.txt','Explicit scope and access limitations'),('sources/regulatory/manifest.json','Regulatory originals, hashes and failed-export status'),('scripts/build_independent_universe.py','Outcome-independent universe reconstruction'),('scripts/build_independent_evidence.py','Curated source extraction and case records')])+'</ul>')
add('<details><summary>Data dictionary</summary>'+table(['Field','Meaning'],[[esc(k),esc(v)] for k,v in e['data_dictionary'].items()])+'</details>')
add('<details><summary>Full retrieved-frame screen (1,442 rows)</summary><input data-filter="frame-table" placeholder="Filter full frame" aria-label="Filter full approval frame">'+table(['ID / product','Date','Disposition','Reason / status'],[[esc(r['id'])+'<br>'+esc(r['product']),esc(r.get('us_approval_date') or 'not adjudicated'),esc(r['classification']),esc(r['reason'])+'<br><small>'+esc(r['classification_status'])+'</small>'] for r in frame],'frame-table')+'</details>')
add('<h2 id="sources">Source registry</h2><p>Inline references support observed statements. Mechanism and CMP transferability judgments are investigator inferences. Reused sources are marked; search leads and unavailable full texts are not represented as original models read.</p><ol class="sources">')
for k,s in e['sources'].items():add('<li id="source-'+esc(k)+'">'+link(k)+' — '+esc(s['locator'])+'. <em>'+esc(s['verification'])+'</em>.</li>')
add('''</ol><footer>Prepared 9 November 2026. Public research repository; publication authorized by the user. Historical forecast study remains separate from CMP-002 valuation. All numerical forecast errors are exploratory unless explicitly stated otherwise.</footer></main><script>document.querySelectorAll('input[data-filter]').forEach(input=>input.addEventListener('input',()=>{const q=input.value.toLowerCase();document.querySelectorAll('.'+input.dataset.filter+' tbody tr').forEach(r=>r.hidden=!r.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(q))}));</script></body></html>''')
